                  <provenance type="#e"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_320">Lincoln, Lincolnshire.
                        Franciscan convent. </orgName><p>Has the convent's distinctive mark, like a
                        figure 2 with a long horizontal tale transected by two vertical strokes, at
                        fol. 2. Also, at fol. 2, 'De communitate fratrum minorum lincoln' 120
                        (cancelled)'; also another pressmark: 'MS.25'. At fol. 5, 'Ex dono fratris
                        Stephani de Lincoln'' and at fol. 166v 'De communitate fratrum minorum
                        lincolnie, ex dono fratris Stephani de Lincoln''; both these inscriptions in
                        the same hand as the ex libris in another book from the convent, Lincoln,
                        Cathedral, MS 41.</p></provenance>
